# docker/caddy/tools.go is the only Go file in the repo and it is never compiled: its blank
# imports exist purely so `go mod tidy` keeps the version catalog in docker/caddy/go.mod. Left
# detectable, it makes GitHub report the repo as containing Go, and CodeQL's default setup adds
# a Go analysis whose autobuild then fails with "no source code seen" -- `go build ./...` finds
# no packages, because the one file is behind the `tools` build tag.
docker/caddy/tools.go -linguist-detectable
